I could not access the private handoff log, so I could not perform or verify browser sign-in, `ui-designer` review, a second full run, or post-handoff cleanup. I signaled the supervisor and observed it exit, but could not verify its teardown report. Independent review found no remaining code defect after failure-path repairs, but returned **INCOMPLETE** for those live gates.

Final local checks passed: 56 toolkit tests, Python compilation, and tracked/untracked whitespace checks. I marked IMP-015 `[!]`, updated recovery notes, and appended the requested summary to `DONE.md`. The fixture scripts and existing IMP-004 work remain uncommitted; there was no push or PR.

A coordinator-accessible, appropriately private disposable-member handoff needs owner authorization before another attempt at the live gates.
